# Project Charter

## Project Name

AI-Enabled Retail Energy Business Intelligence

---

## Project Purpose

The purpose of this project is to explore how modern business intelligence,
data engineering, automation, and artificial intelligence can improve
decision-making within the U.S. retail energy sector.

The project will create an open-source analytical framework using publicly
available and synthetic data.

---

## Background

Retail energy organizations manage large and complex portfolios of customers,
products, contracts, and energy consumption.

Business intelligence plays an important role in transforming operational
and market data into actionable information.

However, traditional reporting often focuses primarily on historical
performance.

This project explores a more integrated approach combining:

- Reliable data pipelines
- Dimensional data modeling
- Standardized business metrics
- Interactive BI
- Data quality monitoring
- AI-assisted development
- AI-assisted business insights

---

## Primary Goal

Develop a reusable BI framework that demonstrates how retail energy data can
be transformed into actionable business intelligence and AI-assisted
decision support.

---

## Business Objectives

The project aims to:

1. Improve visibility into retail energy portfolio performance.
2. Establish standardized and reusable business metrics.
3. Demonstrate effective BI data modeling.
4. Monitor data quality and pipeline health.
5. Improve the efficiency of BI development through AI-assisted workflows.
6. Explore how AI can help translate analytical results into business insights.
7. Create a foundation for future advanced analytics.

